{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" initial=\"start\">\n  <state id=\"start\">\n    <transition event=\"go\" target=\"\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/limit008-state-id-over-name-bound.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":1,"notes":0,"total":1,"warnings":0},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/limit008-state-id-over-name-bound.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":1039,"endLine":5,"startColumn":14,"startLine":5}}}],"message":{"markdown":"state ID `sxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx…` is 1,025 bytes, more than the 1,024 a state name may have\n\n**Note:** every build names the active states by their IDs (each step's configuration, snapshots, `In()`), and a name holds at most 1,024 bytes of UTF-8, so this state could never be reported once entered; SCXML 1.0 §3.14 sets no length, and this is the implementation's bound (spec errata L.6)\n\n**Help:** shorten the ID to at most 1,024 bytes and update every reference to it\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §3.14 IDs","text":"state ID `sxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx…` is 1,025 bytes, more than the 1,024 a state name may have"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":2212,"start":1187},"category":"semantic"},"ruleId":"LIMIT008"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"every build names the active states by their IDs (the configuration each call result reports, snapshots, and `In()`), and a name holds at most 1,024 bytes of UTF-8, so a state with a longer ID could never be reported once entered. A state that can complete (one with a `<final>` child, or a `<parallel>` with a `<state>` region that has a `<final>` child and whose every region can be in a final state at once; SCXML 1.0 Appendix D: a `<parallel>` whose regions are all `<parallel>` never completes) also raises `done.state.<ID>` (SCXML 1.0 §3.7: the processor \"MUST generate the event done.state.id\"), an event name of 11 more bytes, so its ID may have at most 1,013. Lengths are of the ID with its white space collapsed (`xsd:ID`, XML Schema 1.1 Part 2 §4.3.6), as the compiler reads it. SCXML 1.0 §3.14 sets no length; this is the implementation's interface bound, listed in the specification errata (L.6), and it applies to every build"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: shorten the ID to at most 1,024 bytes (1,013 for a state that can complete) and update every reference to it.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §3.14 IDs\n\nRun `scx --explain LIMIT008` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#IDs","id":"LIMIT008","name":"LIMIT008","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"a state ID is longer than a state name may be"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}